example.en:
Practice: For the list 12 → 7 → 25 → 3 → NULL, write a program that counts the nodes and finds their sum and the largest value.

----------------------------------------
public class Traverse {
    static class Node { int data; Node next; Node(int d) { data = d; } }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Node head = new Node(12);
        head.next = new Node(7);
        head.next.next = new Node(25);
        head.next.next.next = new Node(3);
        int count = 0, sum = 0, max = head.data;
        for (Node p = head; p != null; p = p.next) {
            count++;
            sum += p.data;
            if (p.data > max) max = p.data;
        }
        System.out.println("count = " + count + ", sum = " + sum + ", max = " + max);
    }
}
----------------------------------------

Step 1: p = node 12: count = 1, sum = 12, max = 12.
Step 2: p = node 7: count = 2, sum = 19, max stays 12.
Step 3: p = node 25: count = 3, sum = 44, max = 25.
Step 4: p = node 3: count = 4, sum = 47, max stays 25. Then p = NULL, so the loop stops.
Answer: the program prints **count = 4, sum = 47, max = 25**; one pass over the list, O(n).

